# Copy to `.leakterms` (gitignored) and fill in the real terms, one per line.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive.
#
# This file must never contain a real term. `.leakterms` itself must never be
# committed, and must never be encoded-and-committed either: base64 is not
# secrecy, and an earlier version of this repository leaked its whole list that
# way. If a term is sensitive enough to scan for, it is sensitive enough to keep
# out of a public repository entirely.
#
# What belongs here:
#   - retired product or project names that should not resurface
#   - internal process vocabulary, gate names, QA terminology
#   - internal documentation paths
#   - symbol names from private source
#   - third-party internal labels that appeared in private release notes
#
# Where to keep the real list:
#   - locally in .leakterms, and
#   - in CI, as the LEAKSCAN_TERMS secret (newline- or comma-separated)
#
# Without either, `node scripts/leakscan.mjs` reports PARTIAL and
# `scripts/publish.mjs` refuses to publish.
